# Ignore every virtual environment in this folder, keep Requirements/ tracked.
#
# `**` excludes everything at every depth, then the negations carve exceptions
# back out. (A bare `*` behaves the same here — both were verified.)
# Order matters, and so does the middle line: git will not re-include a file
# whose parent directory is still excluded, so `Requirements/` has to be
# un-excluded before `Requirements/**` can match anything inside it.

*

# Without this, the pattern above matches this very file and git refuses to
# track it.
# The rules would still work locally and then vanish on the next clone.
!.gitignore

!Requirements/
!Requirements/**
